, fused relative) Regardless of how; no matter how", "tags": ["not comparable"], "examples": ["However clear you think you've been, and however many questions you may've answered, there'll always remain some doubts.", "Any rule of thumb, however true (it is), is useless unless you understand its underlying logic.", "However much I study, I never get good grades."], "quotes": [{"text": "Elinor, however little concerned in it, joined in their discourse; and Marianne, who had the knack of finding her way in every house to the library, however it might be avoided by the family in general, soon procured herself a book.", "reference": "1811, Jane Austen, Sense and Sensibility, Chapter 42:"}], "synonyms": ["howsoever", "howso", "howsoevermuch"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "por más que"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "aunque más"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "por muy"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(manner, fused relative) Regardless of how; regardless of the way in which.", "tags": ["not comparable"], "examples": ["Let me know when you've had your interview, however it goes.", "However we do this, it isn't going to work."], "quotes": [{"text": "Elinor, however little concerned in it, joined in their discourse; and Marianne, who had the knack of finding her way in every house to the library, however it might be avoided by the family in general, soon procured herself a book.", "reference": "1811, Jane Austen, Sense and Sensibility, Chapter 42:"}, {"text": "But the real way to build a successful online business is to be better than your rivals at undermining people's control of their own attention. Partly, this is a result of how online advertising has traditionally worked: advertisers pay for clicks, and a click is a click, however it's obtained.", "reference": "2013 June 21, Oliver Burkeman, “The tao of tech”, in The Guardian Weekly, volume 189, number 2, page 48:"}], "synonyms": ["howsoever", "howso", "anyhow"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(manner, fused relative) In any way in which; how.", "tags": ["not comparable"], "examples": ["She offered to help however she could.", "Wear your hair however you want."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "comoquiera que"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "como sea que"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "como fuere que"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "como fuese que"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "como fuera que"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "de cualquier manera que"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "de cualquier modo que"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "de cualquier manera que"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(informal, manner) In any way that one likes or chooses; in a haphazard or spontaneous way.", "tags": ["informal", "not comparable"], "examples": ["I don't care; just do it however.", "Nothing was really planned; things just happened however."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "mal que bien"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "bien que mal"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "comoquiera"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "comoquier"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "de cualquier modo"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "de cualquier forma"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "de cualquier manera"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "como sea"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "como fuese"}, 